# Copy to .env.local and adjust. Changes to it need the dev server restarted —
# Turbopack won't pick them up on its own.
#
# `npm run db:push` reads this file too. It goes through drizzle-kit, which only
# loads `.env` on its own, so drizzle.config.ts loads `.env.local` explicitly —
# otherwise it would create the schema somewhere `npm run dev` never looks.

# Where the SQLite file lives. Keep it OUTSIDE the repo: a checkout is
# disposable, and taking your tickets with it when you delete one is
# unrecoverable. The directory must already exist.
#
# macOS / Linux:
DATABASE_FILE=/Users/you/kanban/kanban.db
# Windows — forward slashes, which Node accepts and which avoid having to escape
# backslashes in this file:
# DATABASE_FILE=C:/Users/you/kanban/kanban.db

# Where `npm run db:backup` writes snapshots. Defaults to ~/kanban-backups.
# BACKUP_DIR=/Users/you/kanban-backups

# Optional — Slack pin sync. Leave unset and the feature is simply off.
# A *user* token (xoxp-), not a bot token: reactions.list returns the items the
# authenticated user reacted to, and a bot only ever sees its own reactions.
# scripts/slack-app-manifest.yaml creates an app with the right scopes, and
# `npm run slack:check` verifies the token before the app touches it.
# SLACK_USER_TOKEN=xoxp-...
